				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Jaya",
				Description: "<p>Jaya Island, often simply called Jaya, is a spring island in the middle of Paradise that once was the home of the shandia tribe, before the island was split in half when a Knock-Up Stream sent the island's eastern half soaring into the sky, leaving the rest of the island abandoned and deserted and leading to the famous events from Liar Noland's story.</p><p>Though the island originally looked like a skull, now only the Mouth Bay (マウスべイ) remains, making the original shape harder to visualize. After the island was abandoned for years, a settlement of outlaws called Mock Town arose in its place on its western shore. Its log recording takes four days.</p><p>To the East of what remains of Jaya lies South Grave, a large forest. Its name is actually derived from the fact it was considered a graveyard by the old shandia, who believed that the spirits of their ancestors would return to these sacred trees, marking them as tombstones. The forest currently features a lot of dangerous wildlife that makes it perilous to traverse. North of it, on one of the capes, a sole remaining house of the shandia tribe remains, which Mont Blanc Cricket used as his base of operations.</p>",
