		// 		Description: "<p>Water 7 is a Government affiliated democratic city-state country that is built on Zousenjima, an island that has completely sunk due to rising sea levels, to the point only the top of a man-made plateau on it remains where the city resides, accompanied by parts of the city surrounding the plateau that have been built atop the older sunken buildings. The city is known worldwide for having some of the best shipwrights on the planet, hence why it is located on 'Shipyard Island'.</p><p>Water 7 has embraced its water canals to make use of water for transport and many other needs, becoming known as the 'Capital of Water'. The giant fountain at the center of the island redistributes water across all of its districts. The island is divided into 9 sectors, essentially split up like pizza slices by the large streams of the fountain. On its Northern side is a unique sector that houses the Blue Station, from where all trains depart for the islands of Pucci, San Faldo, St. Poplar, or Enies Lobby. Opposite to it is the sector called the 'Central District', while the remaining seven sectors are occupied by seven 'Docks', going from Dock 1 all the way to Dock 7, giving the island its name.</p><p>Each Dock was originally owned by seven separate shipbuilding companies, until Iceburg united all seven of them into the unified Galley-La Company 7 years ago, which is now headquartered by Dock 1, considered the most elite of them all. Iceburg's efforts have earned him his position as the democratically elected mayor of Water 7, loved by his people. He managed to follow on his master Tom's efforts of getting Water 7 out of an economic recession, with the sea train having restored trade to the island and Iceburg's policies turning Water 7 into a flourishing and peaceful country. He is currently developing a plan to turn Water 7 into a floating island to solve its flood issues. The Franky Family gang led some criminal activity on the island, but they've mostly reformed and been integrated into the Galley-La Company.</p><p>The city and its fountain plateau actually span over 800 years of history in which it has been sinking. The ancient weapon Pluton, a warship capable of wiping entire islands, was said to have originally been built in this city, to then be later handed off to the Wano Country, though its blueprints were kept in secret for centuries until they were recently lost.</p><p>The city is inspired by Venezia, or Venice, in Italy and its canal system, also being built over water and suffering from high tides.</p>",
