    			map: "index.html", 
				japName: "女ヶ島",
				location: "Southern Paradise Calm Belt",
				Image: "./images/Nyogashima.png",
				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Nyogashima",
				Description: "<p>Nyogashima, translating to 'Island of Women', is an island located on the eastern side of the lower Calm Belt of Paradise, directly south-west of Enies Lobby. It is host to the Empire of Amazon Lily, where the kuja race resides, for which the island territory is also occasionally addressed by the same name by extension.</p><p>The island is built around a giant hollow mountain, which houses the settlement within it. Combined with its location in the Calm Belt, this makes it a natural fortress, as it can only be accessed through a heavily fortified gate. Atop the mountain are three great archways, upon which are carved nine snake heads (three for each arch), the namesake of the kuja (nine snakes) race. On the mountain is also engraved the kanji for 'kuja', or 'nine snakes'. On one of the sides outside the mountain is the Arena (闘技場), a coliseum used by the Kuja to entertain their locals with fierce matches.</p><p>After the Marine attack on the island to capture Boa Hancock, Seraphim S-Hawk's attack cut the mountain in half, leaving a side of it exposed.</p>",
