				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Merveille-Archipelago",
				Description: "<p>Merveille, formally the Merveille Archipelago, translating to the Wonders Archipelago, and also known as the 'Strong World', is a collection of islands found in the latter part of Paradise after the Florian Triangle.</p><p>Shiki the Golden Lion made this archipelago his base to develop an army of evolved animals by abusing the extracted effects of the local IQ plant, a plant which can speed up the evolutionary process of creatures when developed. Shiki used his powers to make the archipelago float in the sky, making it a set of floating islands each with different seasons, climates, and layouts, including plenty of spring, summer, fall, and winter Islands. Seen in the movie, atop the highest winter island lay Shiki's ornate fortress known as the Royal Palace (王宮). On one of the islands is also a village of locals, who have developed feathers on their arms that allow them to glide on the air thanks to the powers of the IQ plant.</p><p>Though the events of Strong World are non-canon, the archipelago is canon via Chapter 0. Given Shiki's role being for the sake of the film, the archipelago's fate in canon is not really relevant. The archipelago may be inspired by the Galapagos, as they served as the key for Darwin's theory of evolution due to how animals evolved differently on each island. Shiki's palace is based on traditional Chinese and Japanese architecture.</p>",
