				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Deep-Sea",
				Description: "<p>The Deep Sea, also called the 'Sea Underworld' (海の暗黒街) refers to the area of the sea that composes the lowest reachest of the ocean close to the Sea Floor. This term is also particularly used to refer to the stretch of sea that lies in the path towards Fish-Man Island due to the depth of the Sea Trench, considered to be the connecting sea between Paradise and the New World and found at around 7,000 meters under sea level.</p><p>At these depths, no light comes from the surface, so its local sea life has evolved to survive in this deep darkness, many of which have developed to become incredibly dangerous, making the journey a treacherous trek. Due to its deep pressure, any creature or item that hasn't adapted to live there may also be crushed by the pressure, which is why ships use bubble coating technology to cross it.</p><p>The Deep Sea leading to Fish-Man Island can be accessed via the 'Downward Plume' (下降流のプルーム) a current acting like an undersea waterfall stretching several hundreds of meters which leads directly to the Deep Sea.</p>",
