				Description: "<p>The Red Port refers to one of two ports located on both sides of the Red Line, in the point where it intercepts with the Grand Line.</p><p>Located at the base of the colossal mountain range, the Red Ports are ports artificially built on the edge of the Red Line at sea level with human settlements on it. Given the presence of a few Yarukiman Mangroves like those of the Sabaody Archipelago, resin bubbles are generated and float around the island. This technology has been used to construct Bondolas, bubble gondolas that use the bubbles to propel them up into the air while attached to ropeways, allowing them to essentially function as elevators to scale the Red Line, making access to the Holyland Mary Geoise very restricted and controlled.</p><p>In the Western port which connects to Paradise, the front of a large ship pops out of the Red Line, around which the settlement is built on artificially built platforms. It's unknown what relevance this ship has or how it got incrusted into the Red Line to begin with, but it makes one wonder.</p>",
