				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Marine-HQ",
				Description: "<p>Marine Headquarters is the central base of operations of the Marines, the military navy of the World Government.</p><p>Originally located at the island of Marineford for centuries, it was displaced by Fleet Admiral Sakazuki where the G-1 Base previously was at the entrance of the New World, to keep a tighter leash on the pirates of that sea. The newly built and improved fortress is a massive layered castle in the shape of a hexagon, with a traditional castle built atop. Two large archways sprout from the base, and though one may mistake them for a fast food joint, they are in fact in the shape of a seagull, the symbol of the Marines.</p><p>The Marines are led by a Fleet Admiral, who oversees the movements of the army and is directly subservient to the orders of the Celestial Dragons and the Five Elder Planets. This position was previously held by Kong, Sengoku, and now Sakazuki. Under the Fleet Admiral are the three Admirals, who are so immensely powerful as to act as one of the Government's strongest assets, and below them are Vice-Admirals, Rear Admirals, Commodores, Captains, and so on. Marines from Headquarters hold more value in their rank than those of other bases, so for example a Captain from Headquarters is a far more prestigious position than a captain from a random base. Dozens of Marine Bases are scattered across the world, with those on the Grand Line known as 'G' bases.</p>",
