		// 		Description: "<p>Punk Hazard is an island in the Grand Line, fairly close to the entrance of the New World, though it is hard to locate as no natural log points to the island. It is either a Spring or Summer island given its original temperate weather.</p><p>Originally a circular-shaped island abundant with greenery, Punk Hazard served as the main laboratory of Dr. Vegapunk, who used it to experiment on many of his creations by using Marine prisoners as test subjects. However, four years ago, his subordinate Caesar Clown detonated a gas weapon, causing the entire island to be covered in toxin gas. The Government and researchers evacuated, but the prisoners were abandoned on the island, forced to survive at all costs the debilitating effects of the gas.</p><p>Caesar Clown however escaped imprisonment from the Government and entered service under the broker Joker, returning to Punk Hazard to continue his experiments. There he posed as a savior to the suffering inmates, saving their lives and taking them in as subordinates, referring to him as 'Master'. Over the next three years he would research into many forbidden subjects, such as artificial devil fruits and gigantification among other things, but struggled to make as efficient results as Vegapunk.</p><p>Two years ago, Kuzan and Sakazuki used Punk Hazard as their dueling ground to settle who would become the next Marine Fleet Admiral, unaware of Caesar and his goons hiding on the island during their duel. After a fierce 10 day duel, the entire island was split in half, creating a giant crater in the middle and two canyons leading into it, which became filled with seawater. Furthermore, their devil fruits caused the very climate of the island to shift, with the side Sakazuki stood on becoming incredibly hot and covered in flames and molten lava known as the 'Fire Lands', whereas Kuzan's side became cold and carpeted in snow known as the 'Ice Lands'. After Sakazuki's victory, Caesar went back to his experiments, though now having to adapt to the new climate. That would be until he would be kidnapped by Luffy and Law's alliance, causing the island to become truly deserted once and for all.</p>",
