				japName: "パンクレコーズ",
				location: "Sky",
				Image: "./images/Punk-Records.png",
				Class: "tiny",
				Id:"Punk-Records",
				Description: "<p>Punk Records is an artificial sky island composed by what was originally the top side of Egghead's Labophase.</p><p>Originally, Punk Records referred to the top building of the Labophase in the shape of a large eggshell, with a set of floating blocks being held aloft around it through anti-gravity. Within the eggshell is a large room housing Vegapunk's brain, which he cut off from his main body after it got too big, now referring to it as 'Punk Records', a name used for both the brain system and the whole area itself. Vegapunk's clones, the Punks, can connect to this brain wirelessly and share their memories together.</p><p>After the Egghead Incident, Edison used the Fabiriophase's Cloudfter to turn Punk Records into its own separate artificial sky island, to make it escape from the clutches of the Government. The plan was to make the entire Labophase fly away, but York was able to separate the two, keeping the Vegapunk Labo on Egghead. Punk Records now flies the skies in hiding, requesting the aid of Weatheria. Aside from the brain, some facilities are located within the eggshell, such as a room with replacement parts, but not enough material is found there to continue research in earnest as the Punks did back in the Labo.</p><p>Punk Records might potentially be inspired by the billboard of Tower Records, a famous music shop building found in Shibuya and an iconic landmark of the city.</p>",
