				Description: "<p>Hachinosu (translating to 'Beehive'), also known by its alias of Kaizokujima (translating to 'Pirate Island'), with both names being used completely interchangeably and occasionally sometimes together, is a seemingly summer island located somewhere in the middle to late area of the New World, found less than a day away from the Egghead sea area.</p><p>As a rocky tropical island, Hachinosu is defined by the gigantic mountain in its center carved in the shape of a pirate skull, which houses a castle within its stone, inside of which is its throne room. Surrounding it are several decrepit buildings that dot the island's hill. Thanks to his devil fruit, Avalo Pizarro has become able to take control of the entire island, making its skull come to life. Somewhere within the island is known to be found a Poneglyph.</p><p>Originally starting as a penal territory, for which it was also known as 'Exile Island' (流刑島, Rukeijima), it was treated as a deserted island where the world's worst criminals from many different countries were sent to in order to starve when no other prisons in the world could handle them. However, once a gold deposit was found there, surviving pirates banded together and worked together with an Underworld organization to attain great wealth, eventually building on Hachinosu a lawless pirate country, ruled by a leader who holds the position of 'Commodore' (提督), occasionally also referred to as 'King'. Though pirates will often clash and even kill each other on the island due to its lawlessness, they tend to leave those working on the island's establishments since they rely on their work, and there are still some general rules they are all expected to follow. When Shakky opened up a bar on the island, she came to be known as the island's 'treasure'.</p><p>Long ago, the Davy Back Fight, a game for recruiting pirates from other crews named after the legendary pirate Davy Jones, was invented on this island. Four decades ago, the legendarily powerful pirate Rocks D. Xebec took over the island to keep growing his powerful pirate crew, but after his supposed death at God Valley 38 years ago, one of his crewmates, Ouchoku, became Hachinosu's Commodore, until the Rocky Port incident 2 years ago where Trafalgar Law staged the theft of the hearts of 100 pirates from the island when hijacking the ship Rocky Port, in order to secure a position as a Warlord. During this same incident, the Marine Koby came to be known as a 'Hero', while Blackbeard dethroned Ouchoku to make Hachinosu his new base and become its Admiral and King, but he holds further plans to turn it into a Government affiliated country called the 'Blackbeard Kingdom' (黒ひげ王国).</p><p>The name Hachinosu, meaning 'Beehive', refers to how the island is swarming with pirates as if they were bees. A wise saying warns one to 'never poke the beehive'. Hachinosu was likely inspired by real life pirate gathering spots like the island of Tortuga in the Caribbean.</p>",
