				Class: "middle",
				Id:"Loguetown",
				Description: "<p>Loguetown is a Government affiliated port town located on the larger island of the Pole Star Archipelago, on its south-western side.</p><p>It is the town where the Pirate King Gol D. Roger was born, grew up through a difficult childhood, and where he was eventually executed 24 years ago, marking this place as the start of the Great Pirate Era. As such, it is known as the 'Town of Beginnings and Endings' (始まりと終わりの町), referring to prologues and epilogues.</p><p>Serving as a popular spot for those entering the Grand Line, this bustling town blooms with beautiful architecture and many vibrant shops, with many of its inhabitants sporting trendy and fashionable clothes. At a central square is the execution scaffolding where Roger was killed, which now serves as a historical landmark. An illustrious hotel built to house royalty traveling to the Levely has a direct view of the platform. The town also has a Marine base to prevent pirates from swarming into the Grand Line, which was originally operated by Smoker, and also has its own local police force.</p><p>Loguetown's design and architecture were inspired by Firenze, or Florence, in Italy, with its main distinguishing feature, its large church dome, being identical to that found there.</p>",
