				Class: "middle",
				Id:"Reverse-Mountain",
				Description: "<p>Reverse Mountain is a mountain of the Red Line continent that was originally a winter island, being located at the point where the Red Line and Grand Line intersect, at the antipodes of Mary Geoise.</p><p>Reverse Mountain is a mountain of over 3000 meters where four rivers run in from each of the Blues and one into Paradise. The weather of the island generates currents which cause its rivers to flow in reverse, upward instead of downward, allowing ships to sail up the mountain, with all four canals from the Blues leading to the top and flowing down the river which grants access into Paradise, making this one of the main ways of accessing the Grand Line./p>",
