				Description: "<p>The Hokkyoku, or North Pole, refers to the northernmost point of the planet upon which the World rotates on its axis, though the term is also generally used to refer to the surrounding geographical area. It is located on the Red Line between the North Blue and East Blue.</p><p>Famous for being a very cold place, the North Pole is also known for having a colony of krakens, colossal octopi of around 300m in length when stretched. It is the place from where the kraken Surume originates from before he was abducted by Hody Jones.</p><p>Some have debated whether the poles are on the Red Line or not due to geographic coordinates given at some points, but according to Oda's own notes, they are depicted as being on the Red Line, with the specific position being those shown on this map. These notes also include a drawing of the planet spinning on its axis with the poles being clearly shown on the Red Line. This drawing was misinterpreted by some as representing a pole shift, but the note indicates it is depicting the 23.5 degree axis tilt the planet has respective to its revolution around the Sun (which is the same as Earth), as the spinning pattern can be observed in the drawing. Nonetheless, the matter still remains disputed among some scholars given certain cardinal directions provided in the series.</p>",
