				Description: "<p>The Mokomo Dukedom, translating to 'Fluffy Dukedom', is a non-Government independent duchy located on what is called Zou Island atop the back of the titanic elephant Zunesha.</p><p>Mokomo operates as a duchy working under the Kouzuki Clan of the Wano Country, with whom they've sworn a historical pact of brotherhood. It is composed by the mink race, hominids with an appearance between humans and furred animals, who possess their own customs and traditions, such as very intimate skinship accompanied by the greeting 'garchuu', as well as a local dialect of the Koyogo language that tends to add the words 'teia' or 'gara' to pronouns.</p><p>The mink are also trained in 'electro', a technique where they use static electricity to generate electrical shockwaves. Due to their isolationist policy, having closed their borders from the World Government like many other races to protect the lode poneglyph they hide, they have cut off contact from humans and are all trained warriors from birth. Though this has sparked bad rumors regarding them, they are still friendly towards humans and other races; they are simply protective of those that may try to subjugate them. This long-standing peace was briefly disturbed when Jack of the Beasts Pirates invaded the island, ruining much of the ancient city, but ultimately the mink race persevered and recovered.</p><p>The duchy is ruled by a Duke, though sometimes also called a 'King', the one 26 years ago being Duke Hitsugisukan. He was followed by Inuarashi and Nekomamushi, who due to a dispute were unable to settle who should be Duke, and so adopted a dual Duke system where one would rule over the day and one over the night, from 6:00PM to 6:00AM and viceversa. Following their victory in Wano, Carrot was anointed as the new singular King of Zou. It has also been alluded that Wanda is related to Inuarashi, as she seemed very close with him and was also the owner of Mokomo's national treasure: a purple-colored dress she exchanged with Nami.</p><p>The large buildings around the Dukedom are inspired by those in Naqsh-e, Iran.</p>",
