				Class:"tiny sabaody",
				Id:"Corrida-Coliseum",
				Description: "<p>The Corrida Coliseum, translating into the Bullfighting Coliseum, is a historical building located in Dress Rosa, serving as an arena for gladiators to fight in for the entertainment of the public.</p><p>The Coliseum is located in the Royal Plateau region, right beneath the colossal structure. Within this building, gladiators would fight in its large arena for glory or prizes to the amusement of the audience sitting in the stands, a cultural traditional that spans far in the past. During Doflamingo's rule, combat to the death was re-established, while also keeping many gladiators imprisoned within the building, where Diamante would manage the Coliseum during his rule. After the birdcage incident, the building was heavily damaged. Within the Coliseum is found:</p><p>- The Participants' Waiting Room (選手の控え室) is a room where gladiators would wait before deploying onto the arena, outfitted with punching backs and other items to help them pass the time.</p><p>- The Battle Preparation Room (戦闘準備室) is a room outfitted with all kinds of weapons for the participants. It is seemingly located on the higher level of the Coliseum. At the center of the room is a giant statue of Kyros, the legendary 'King of Gladiator' that won 3000 matches at the Coliseum, but was forgotten after he turned into a toy. The statue was later moved to an open area within Dress Rosa alongside Noland's statue as well as a statue of Luffy and Usopp.</p><p>- The Gladiators' Quarters (剣闘士の宿舎) is an area where local Gladiators were kept within the Coliseum, though it is more of a prison being formed by several cells. During Riku's rule, only prisoners and criminals were kept here, but during Doflamingo's rule, some of his enemies were kept in here under far poorer conditions, and forced to fight under the condition of only being liberated after winning 1000 fights.</p><p>- The Medical Room (医療室) is a room located underground where gladiators are treated after to recover from their battle injuries. However, many gladiators here who are deemed worthy of their potential are sent straight to the Scrap Heap beneath Dress Rosa to be turned into toys.</p><p>- The Family Waiting Room (ファミリー待機室) is a room with a great view of the arena, which was used exclusively by members of the Donquixote Family. Several other waiting rooms, as well as lavatories, are also found across the Coliseum.</p><p>The Corrida Coliseum's design is modeled after Rome's Colosseum, the historical wonder built during the period of ancient Rome, where gladiators would similarly fight for the entertainment of people. At the same time, it is also inspired by corrida arenas in Spain, which are similarly-shaped coliseums where the country's traditional bullfighting performances would take place, hence its name. Fittingly, the Coliseum's symbol is that of a bull.</p>",
